PATCH 329: the MGAVIDEO pitch-cache STATE STORE-WIDTH (DGROUP:0x794 / 0x796) -- patch 326's second root:
`mov ds:0x796,ax` was emitted as a 4-byte store and wiped word[DGROUP:0x798], the head of the pitch->
rowtable MRU free list, so any non-320 viewport pitch made FUN_0000_02c1 `rep stosw` 200 words at
DGROUP:0x0000 -> the documented DGROUP[0x000..0x18f] block-zero -> STRSEG word[DGROUP:0x70] = 0.

ASM (re_out/fist_mga_image.bin; driver DS=ES=DGROUP=0x1c00) -- every access to both slots is a WORD:
    0x2c1: a3 96 07           mov ds:0x796,ax           ; opcode A3 = mov moffs16,ax  (02c1 entry)
    0x2c9: c7 06 94 07 c8 07  mov WORD PTR ds:0x794,0x7c8  ; the pitch==0x140 shortcut
    0x2f1: a3 94 07           mov ds:0x794,ax           ; publish the found node's rowtable offset
Ghidra typed `_DAT_1000_c794` / `_DAT_1000_c796` `undefined4`.  `_DAT_1000_c796 = param_1` therefore wrote
0x796..0x799, clobbering word[DGROUP:0x798] -- the head link of the 8-node free list FUN_0000_0284 builds
(patch 326) -- to 0 on the FIRST 02c1 call (watchpoint-confirmed: `0284` sets word[0x798]=0x79e at
mode-set, then the very next `02c1(param_1=320)` from 024f/00e8 sets it to 0).  `_DAT_1000_c794 = 0x7c8`
likewise wrote over 0x796 (the current pitch).

WHY IT MATTERS (the failure chain, runtime-traced end-to-end):
  free list head = 0  ->  02c1's walk (asm 0x2d3 `mov dx,[bx]; or dx,dx; je 0x2f5`) terminates at the HEAD
  CELL itself (cur = 0x798)  ->  the build path (asm 0x2f5) takes `di = [bx+4]` = word[DGROUP:0x79c] = 0 as
  the node's rowtable buffer and `rep stosw`s 200 words at DGROUP:0x0000  ->  the deterministic
  DGROUP[0x000..0x18f] block-zero patch 326 documents  ->  the engine STRSEG word[DGROUP:0x70] goes
  0x2d74 -> 0  ->  the object-roster RENDER dispatch FUN_0000_c4df (`mov gs,[0x70]; call [gs:bx+0x358a]`,
  patch 292) reads its per-class method vector out of ENGINE CODE at linear 0x358a instead of the real
  table at STRSEG:0x358a (image 0x30cca = c5fc c5fc c5fc c5fc c694 c66e ...)  ->  it dispatches whatever
  code byte pair it finds (e.g. classid 0x10 -> `8b 1e 20 57` -> vector 0x2057 = FUN_0000_2057, the
  sprite-draw node walker) with garbage args -> SIGSEGV.
Patch 326 fixed 0284's free-list node LINKS (the list is now built correctly); this fixes the store that
then WIPED it.  The MENU never requests a non-320 pitch (02c1 short-circuits at `cmp ax,0x140`), which is
why the block-zero is mission-only and why the 24 menu/settings flows never saw it.

The rest of the driver already treats both slots as WORDs (the mode-set init `mov ds:0x794,0x7c8` /
`mov ds:0x796,0x140` and the blit reads `[0x794]` row-table base / `[0x796]`-cx pitch skip), so the
`undefined4` typing was internally inconsistent as well.  Retyping to `undefined2` also fixes the three
readers at 0x2e2's tail / the two blitters, which had been reading `word[0x794] | word[0x796]<<16`.

MISSION-PATH ONLY -> behaviour-neutral for the 24 menu/settings verify flows (verified native 24/24 +
wasm 24/24, native<->wasm 0-diff).
--- a/fist_mga.c
+++ b/fist_mga.c
@@ -640,8 +640,24 @@
 #define _DAT_1000_c788 (*(undefined4 *)(g_mem+0x1c788))
 #define _DAT_1000_c78c (*(undefined4 *)(g_mem+0x1c78c))
 #define _DAT_1000_c792 (*(undefined4 *)(g_mem+0x1c792))
-#define _DAT_1000_c794 (*(undefined4 *)(g_mem+0x1c794))
-#define _DAT_1000_c796 (*(undefined4 *)(g_mem+0x1c796))
